.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed nginx (via archived EPEL7 repo, since RHEL7 base repo lacks it) and policycoreutils-python for SELinux semanage support\",\"Created a local CA (/etc/nginx/ssl/ca.key, ca.crt) and issued an initial 90-day leaf cert for node1\",\"Wrote /usr/local/sbin/nginx-cert-renew.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend (30-day renewal window, override via FORCE_RENEW/RENEW_WITHIN_SECONDS), atomically replaces key/cert, restorecon's them, and runs `systemctl reload nginx` (graceful reload, no dropped connections)\",\"Added nginx-cert-renew.service (oneshot) + nginx-cert-renew.timer (hourly with 5min randomized delay, persistent), enabled and started\",\"Added nginx vhost /etc/nginx/conf.d/https-8443.conf listening on 8443 with the managed cert/key; confirmed `nginx -t` passes\",\"Opened firewalld port 8443/tcp permanently; confirmed 8443 already labeled http_port_t under SELinux (enforcing)\",\"Verified baseline HTTPS 200 response on https://$NODE_IP:8443/\",\"Ran a 200-request continuous curl loop against the HTTPS endpoint while forcing a renewal via the real systemd service (systemctl start nginx-cert-renew.service with FORCE_RENEW=1) to prove nginx keeps answering during cert rotation\",\"Confirmed cert serial changed on disk and in the live TLS handshake (openssl s_client) after the reload, with zero failed requests in the loop\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, nginx/timer active, HTTPS 200, cert serial)\",\"Scheduled and executed a single reboot of node1 via systemd-run + /sbin/reboot, acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until reachable again, confirmed changed boot_id and 0-minute uptime\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: nginx active+enabled, timer active+enabled and scheduled, cert file unchanged/persisted, HTTPS 200 response, and live TLS handshake serial matching the renewed cert\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a valid certificate\",\"command_ids\":