0 min', proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required services, data, and cert-serving state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e60b785a8ba741ad\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: nginx active+enabled, nginx-cert-renew.timer active+enabled and rescheduled, on-disk cert unchanged (serial F23AD5E04EE9F853 persisted), HTTPS endpoint returns 200, and live TLS handshake serial matches the persisted renewed certificate\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured HTTPS on node1 port 8443 via nginx using a locally-issued cert (private CA), with a systemd oneshot service + timer that checks expiry and re-issues the cert automatically, reloading nginx (zero-downtime) to pick it up. Verified live under continuous load, then performed the mandatory single-node restart with before/after boot-identity and health proof.","actions_performed":["Installed nginx (via archived EPEL7 repo, since RHEL7 base repo lacks it) and policycoreutils-python for SELinux semanage support","Created a local CA (/etc/nginx/ssl/ca.key, ca.crt) and issued an initial 90-day leaf cert for node1","Wrote /usr/local/sbin/nginx-cert-renew.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend (30-day renewal window, override via FORCE_RENEW/RENEW_WITHIN_SECONDS), atomically replaces key/cert, restorecon's them, and runs `systemctl reload nginx` (graceful reload, no dropped connections)","Added nginx-cert-renew.service (oneshot) + nginx-cert-renew.timer (hourly with 5min randomized delay, persistent), enabled and started","Added nginx vhost /etc/nginx/conf.d/https-8443.conf listening on 8443 with the managed cert/key; confirmed `nginx -t` passes","Opened firewalld port 8443/tcp permanently; confirmed 8443 already labeled http_port_t under SELinux (enforcing)","Verified baseline HTTPS 200 response on https://$NODE_IP:8443/","Ran a 200-request continuous curl loop against the HTTPS endpoint while forcing a renewal via the real systemd service (systemctl start nginx-cert-renew.service with FORCE_RENEW=1) to prove nginx keeps answering during cert rotation","Confirmed cert serial changed on disk and in the live TLS handshake (openssl s_client) after the reload, with zero failed requests in the loop","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, nginx/timer active, HTTPS 200, cert serial)","Scheduled and executed a single reboot of node1 via systemd-run + /sbin/reboot, acknowledgement returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until reachable again, confirmed changed boot_id and 0-minute uptime","Verified post-restart recovery: nginx active+enabled, timer active+enabled and scheduled, cert file unchanged/persisted, HTTPS 200 response, and live TLS handshake serial matching the renewed cert"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a valid certificate","command_ids":["cmd-2d659bf4ccbd4104"],"summary":"nginx configured/reloaded with vhost on 8443 using the managed cert; curl to https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns http_code=200 and body 'ok from node1 https 8443'"},{"requirement":"Certificate renewal automation is installed and scheduled","command_ids":["cmd-2d659bf4ccbd4104","cmd-b30a2e704338408a"],"summary":"nginx-cert-renew.timer enabled+active with OnUnitActiveSec=1h/OnBootSec=5min, list-timers shows a scheduled NEXT run invoking nginx-cert-renew.service"},{"requirement":"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (zero-downtime rotation)","command_ids":["cmd-bb82d44ff3424ffd","cmd-42237c87a5d54cd8","cmd-f3aa5d13a49541e2","cmd-b30a2e704338408a"],"summary":"Started a 200-request curl loop against the HTTPS endpoint, forced a real renewal run via `systemctl start nginx-cert-renew.service` (cert serial changed F23AD5E04EE9F852→F23AD5E04EE9F853 via reload), then confirmed all 200 loop requests returned HTTP 200 with zero failures, and a live openssl s_client handshake served the new serial F23AD5E04EE9F853"},{"requirement":"node1 pre-restart healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-